WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.750
You all know that.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:06.439
I always say don't DFI politicians, these
are just people.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.420
They are flawed people.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.810
Sometimes they want to do things we agree
with.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.650
Sometimes they don't.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.810
But the idea of holding politicians up and
I don't care if it's the Magga crowd or Bernie

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.220
or bust or the Tulsi people or whoever.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:27.930
I don't recommend defying any politician,
but that doesn't mean that there can be real

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.710
material, important differences between one
politician and another.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.969
And the civil unrest and protests that we've
been seeing this week are providing a really

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.280
good case study to look at some of the differences.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.890
Donald Trump sat at the White House tweeting,
threatening to deploy the military to states.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:53.250
And on one day this week, used police to gas
protesters and used horses to disperse protesters

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.309
so that he could walk over to St. John's and
get a picture.

00:00:56.309 --> 00:00:57.710
Awkwardly holding a Bible.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.060
That's what Trump did.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.679
Meanwhile, Joe Biden and Nancy Pelosi and
Elizabeth Warren have actually gone and met

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:08.939
with protesters and talked to protesters and
even marched with protesters in some cases.

00:01:08.939 --> 00:01:10.909
This doesn't make them perfect people.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:14.140
It doesn't make Democrats uber progressive.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.680
It doesn't make them gods.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.810
It doesn't do anything other than show us.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.439
There is a really stark contrast right now
in terms of how completely out of his element,

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:26.470
an impotent Donald Trump is, how unable to
lead.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:30.790
The president is that he can't even do the
simple things that many elected officials

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.790
are doing.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:36.490
Yesterday, Nancy Pelosi, as we are showing
you on video, went out to the protests in

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:43.340
Washington, D.C., spoke to protesters, walked
around, was part of what was going on.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.810
Doesn't mean anything in particular about
Nancy Pelosi's policy positions.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:53.860
But it does tell us that she's at least out
there seeing what's going on and talking to

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:54.860
people.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.900
Does this make Nancy Pelosi some progressive
change maker?

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:04.979
Now, she's a moderately left establishment
Democrat, but Trump is hiding out and tweeting.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:05.979
OK.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:07.200
It's the contrast that matters.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.830
Yesterday, I told you about Democratic Massachusetts
Senator Elizabeth Warren.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:16.069
She went out to participate in a march on
the streets in Washington, D.C., brought her

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.950
husband along, brought her dog along.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.320
We're showing our video audience some video
of that right now.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.090
And again, making it very clear she was asked,
why is Trump sending out the military?

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.019
She said, well, because he's wrong.

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:32.830
Joining protesters, talking to people, being
out there, being part of our community rather

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.709
than someone sitting at the White House in
the Oval Office or even, you know, in a bunker,

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:41.550
as Donald Trump did did briefly on Friday,
sending out tweets and mobilizing forces and

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.610
putting up fence after fence after fence,
as I don't know if you saw, but significant

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:49.459
new fencing being erected around the White
House area.

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:54.709
Likewise, Democratic presidential candidate
Joe Biden going out even earlier than Nancy

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:58.459
Pelosi, even earlier than Elizabeth Warren
to talk to protesters to understand what's

00:02:58.459 --> 00:02:59.700
going on.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.020
Making a speech about the systemic elements
that are at play and what these protests are

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.730
meant to illuminate.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:13.130
And a deal with Biden, Pelosi and Warren do
not deserve our support just because they

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.500
met with protesters.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.080
We still need to be thinking critically about
every single one of these individuals and

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.080
who we vote for.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:24.080
But the point is there is an absolute total
minimum as public officials that should be

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.780
done just to show you're even remotely engaged
with what's going on out there.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.090
It is about contrast with Donald Trump.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.950
Trump stayed at the White House and tweeted
insults.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.400
He went to his bunker.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.349
He walked over to a church and held up a Bible
that Ivana Trump carried over for him in a

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:43.519
fifteen hundred dollar purse for a photo op
after protesters were dispersed with smoke

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:45.040
and huge horses.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.110
There's just no comparison in terms of how
unfit to lead the president is.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.040
This is just the latest, latest example.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.329
Now, let's deal with some of the critiques.

00:03:54.329 --> 00:03:59.239
Many of you might no doubt say K. Biden, Warren
and Pelosi.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.379
They went out there.

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:02.849
But what have they actually done?

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:04.670
And that's a fair question.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.069
Biden's not even in an elected position right
now.

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:11.440
So what can he do other than say, here's what
I would do as president?

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.549
But they are actually there.

00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:18.940
They're in the midst of what's happening compared
to our easily trigger able president who can't

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:24.010
even be bothered to do any work at this point,
never mind engage with the problems that the

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:28.410
country is dealing with in a way that doesn't
seem patronizing or that will actually make

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.530
the problem worse.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:35.650
I keep going back to one of the thoughts I
keep going back to as the protests started

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:41.010
because of anger about treatment of black
men by police.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.080
Police using too much.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.350
Horse police being too brutal.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:49.510
And what Donald Trump does is say, hey, you
know what, the governors aren't deploying

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.590
enough law enforcement force.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.340
They're not doing enough shows of strength.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:05:01.310
I'm going to override them and send in the
military as if more law enforcement force

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:07.890
is the solution to protests, protesting about
too much law enforcement force being used.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.660
It's inconceivable.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:15.730
There is it's hard to think of someone more
poorly suited to lead at this point in time.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.570
Corona virus already proved it.

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.830
The protests are only the latest example.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.980
And we've got five months.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:23.980
We've got five months.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:06:37.750
And we are ultimately going to decide what
happens next.

